grund config — inspect the effective `grund.toml` discovered from a path.

Usage:  grund config <show | validate> [PATH]
        grund config migrate --to 2 [PATH] [--write] [--drop-comments]

  show       print the effective config as TOML (defaults filled in for keys you didn't set).
  validate   parse the discovered config and report the first error; exit 0 if it's well-formed.
  migrate    print the version-2 file that means what this version-1 config means, and report where each key went;
             writes nothing unless --write is given.

Options:
  --to 2               migrate: the version to migrate to; required, and 2 is the only one.
                       e.g. grund config migrate --to 2
  --write              migrate: replace the config with the candidate, once both comparisons pass.
                       e.g. grund config migrate --to 2 --write
  --drop-comments      migrate: let --write drop the comments the preview lists, and name them again.
                       e.g. grund config migrate --to 2 --write --drop-comments
  --path-base project|invocation
                       project (default) spells report paths from the config root;
                       invocation: relative to the path you passed, or the current directory if you passed none.
                       e.g. grund config show docs/ --path-base=invocation
                       --path-base=invocation replaces a committed `[output] relative_paths = false`.

PATH defaults to `.`; config is discovered by walking up from it — the root `grund.toml` is the home, `.agents/grund.toml` a deprecated fallback.
There is no `--config <file>` override: it is discovered, not pointed at.

Exit:  0 well-formed / printed / migrated · 1 `validate` found an error, or `migrate` refused · 2 no subcommand, or the config couldn't be read.

Examples:
  grund config show               # the effective config, defaults filled in
  grund config validate           # exit 1 if the discovered config has an error
  grund config show docs/         # the config that governs docs/
  grund config migrate --to 2     # the version-2 file, previewed; nothing written
